Consider the given two statements:
<table border="1" cellpadding="1" cellspacing="1"><tbody><tr><td><span style="white-space:nowrap;"><strong>Statement I: </strong></span></td><td style="text-align: justify;">A molar property (Xₘ) is the value of an extensive property (X) of a system for 0.1 mol of a substance.&nbsp;</td></tr><tr><td><span style="white-space:nowrap;"><strong>Statement II: </strong></span></td><td style="text-align: justify;">If n is the amount of substance, then Xₘ = X/n and Xₘ is independent of the amount of substance.</td></tr></tbody></table><br>Choose the correct answer among the given options:&nbsp;
<table border="1" cellpadding="1" cellspacing="1"><tbody><tr><td>1.</td><td><strong>Statement I</strong> is correct; <strong>Statement II</strong> is correct.</td></tr><tr><td>2.</td><td><strong>Statement I</strong> is incorrect; <strong>Statement II</strong> is incorrect.</td></tr><tr><td>3.</td><td><strong>Statement I</strong> is correct; <strong>Statement II</strong> is incorrect.</td></tr><tr><td>4.</td><td><strong>Statement I </strong>is incorrect; <strong>Statement II</strong> is correct.</td></tr></tbody></table>
